```php
interface NotificationChannel { public function send(User $u, Message $m): void; }

abstract class TemplatedChannel implements NotificationChannel {
    protected function formatMessage(Message $m): string { /* shared */ }
}

class EmailChannel extends TemplatedChannel { public function send(User $u, Message $m): void { /* uses formatMessage */ } }
class PushChannel implements NotificationChannel { /* no template needed */ }

The interface is the contract every channel must meet (so a Notifier can accept any); the abstract class removes duplication for those that share formatting. Push skips the abstract class — proof you shouldn't force everything into one hierarchy.
